; WildGrass — Wild grass terrain visual. Emits NOTHING; deliberately tag-inert, and that
; inertness is load-bearing (terrain.md). This is what untouched revealed land looks like, and
; spec.md Open Question #29 is still open on it: it must read as "something to claim" without
; reading as broken.
;
; STILL EXACTLY ONE VARIANT, AND THAT IS A DELIBERATE HOLD, NOT AN OMISSION. Meadow and Scrub
; each went to 3 variants in this pass; Wild grass did not, because its `model_scenes` count is
; not a look decision here — it is wired into behaviour. `wild_grass` is one of only two style
; PICKER categories, so a second variant would make `WorldRoot._supports_mixed()` true, put a
; `mixed` row at the head of its catalog, and move its unchosen default off "wild_grass" onto
; "mixed" for every existing save (the same consequence D-54 accepted for Forest, but never
; ruled on for this terrain). Four test assertions pin the current state deliberately —
; test_hud_hotbar.gd's `style_ids_for_category("wild_grass").size() == 1`, two stale-id
; fallbacks in test_style_defaults.gd and one in test_save_round_trip.gd.
;
; RULED 2026-09-08 -> D-56: "wild grass should only have a single type". This is now a STANDING
; CONSTRAINT, not an unfinished look pass. Do not add a second variant here without a fresh
; human ruling, and do not re-point those four assertions to make one fit — they are the guard
; on that decision, not stale scaffolding. Improving this terrain's LOOK is still fair game
; (Open Question #29 is untouched and open); doing it by adding a variant is not.
;
; REBUILT THROUGH THE SHARED GENERATOR (2026-09-08) with its own values carried over unchanged:
; slab Color(0.55, 0.52, 0.3) olive-khaki, 3 bare-dirt patches, Grass_Common_Short at the
; shorter 0.065 baseline, seed 20260816. THE COUNT AND THE PATCH TINT HAVE SINCE MOVED — see
; the 2026-09-08 notes below; the 0.065 height baseline and the seed are unchanged.
;
; CLUSTERED, NOT EVENLY SCATTERED, and this is the one place the shared generator's scatter is
; overridden: the blades are distributed across 8 uneven clump centres (18/8/14/10/16/8/12/10)
; with real bare ground between them. An even scatter would read as a mown lawn, which is precisely the
; opposite of "untouched" — the distinction from true Grass is the whole job of this tile.
;
; SCATTER RELAID 2026-09-08 (human report: "looks very repetitive since it only has a small
; amount of grass in the middle of the tile"). THE CLUMPING ABOVE IS INTACT; WHAT CHANGED IS
; WHERE THE CLUMPS SIT. The 2026-08-16 clump override had constrained its centres so tightly
; that all 32 blades fell within +/-0.279 of centre — the middle ~56% of the tile — making this
; the ONLY tile in the grass family that failed to reach the +/-0.42 envelope the rest of it
; uses (GrassCommonShort +/-0.418, GrassClover +/-0.414, Meadow +/-0.413, Snowfield +/-0.414,
; Scrub +/-0.399). Consequences, both of which the report is describing:
;
;   * SEAM BAND. Two abutting tiles leave a bare strip of 2 * (0.5 - reach) centred on their
;     shared seam. At +/-0.42 that strip is 0.16 and every other terrain already lives with it;
;     at +/-0.279 it was 0.44 — nearly a whole tile width of bare slab ringing every tile, which
;     is what drew the grid. It is now 0.160/0.160, i.e. at the floor the envelope allows.
;   * The 3 bare-dirt patches had all landed in the SAME quadrant (x -0.06..-0.19,
;     z -0.07..-0.18), stamping an identical dark smudge in the identical corner of every tile
;     in the world. They are now spread with a minimum separation.
;
; Clump centres are placed on a jittered RING, deliberately not a 2x2 quadrant grid: quadrants
; put the gaps between clumps on the two axes, leaving an axis-aligned bare cross through the
; tile centre, and a bare cross repeated on every tile is the same lattice again shifted half a
; tile. Because clumping and seam coverage pull against each other, the layout is CHOSEN rather
; than merely drawn — the generator draws candidates from the one seeded stream, keeps those
; reaching the seam floor, and among them takes the MOST CLUMPED (this one measures 0.67 on
; mean-nearest-neighbour over uniform, so it is still visibly patchy, not a lawn). Patchiness
; therefore lands in the tile INTERIOR, where a gap reads as meadow, instead of on the seam,
; where a gap reads as a grid line.
;
; DENSITY RAISED TO 96 BLADES, AND THE PATCHES TONED DOWN (2026-09-08, second and third
; rounds of the same human report). Round two: "it still does not look random when multiple
; tiles are next to each other ... there just aren't enough tufts of grass" — so the count went
; 32 -> 96 and the clumps 4 -> 8. This supersedes the 2026-08-16 count of 32, which that day's
; feedback had itself raised from 4. DENSITY IS THE REAL ANTI-REPETITION LEVER: one scene per
; tile (-> D-56) is a lattice by construction and relaying the scatter cannot change that; what
; changes is whether the eye can RESOLVE the repeating unit. Sparse tufts make each tile a
; readable little arrangement you can match against its neighbour; dense ones read as continuous
; ground cover. Variants are the other way out of a lattice and D-56 closed that, so density is
; the lever that is left.
;
; Round three came from a screenshot, and it corrected the diagnosis: THE BARE-DIRT PATCHES WERE
; THE LOUDEST REPEAT, NOT THE GRASS. Flat, hard-edged, axis-aligned quads in a dark brown
; (0.42, 0.34, 0.2) on an olive slab (0.55, 0.52, 0.3) is a big enough contrast step that the
; eye locks onto the three stamps and reads their positions as the grid, while tufts close to
; the slab in hue register as noise beside them. They are now blended 35% of the way from slab
; toward that brown — Color(0.5045, 0.457, 0.265) — a soft mottle rather than a stamp. Removal
; was NOT the fix: the patches still earn their place as "untended, patchy ground", they just
; must not out-shout the grass. It is a look dial; `PATCH_CONTRAST_BLEND` in the generator.
;
; STILL ONE VARIANT (-> D-56): this rewrites the single scene's contents and adds nothing to
; `model_scenes`, so `_supports_mixed()` stays false and the four assertions pinning the variant
; count are untouched. Open Question #29 is unaffected and still open.
;
; BUILT BY A SCRIPT, NOT HAND-AUTHORED, AND NOT EDITABLE BY HAND — same buffer layout and
; headless caveat as the four Grass variants; see GrassCommonShort.tscn's header for the full
; explanation. The generator this file's header used to point at was a one-off that was never
; committed; it now exists and is re-runnable as `scripts/generate_wild_grass_scatter.py`, which
; carries the full reasoning for every constant. Re-run it to change anything below; do not
; hand-edit the MultiMesh buffer or the FloorPatch transforms.
;
; INHERITS THE GRASS CALIBRATION BASELINE (human sign-off 2026-09-08): slab BoxMesh
; 1.0 x 0.2 x 1.0 at y=-0.1 (the 1.0 width is the cross-tile seam-gap fix, do not narrow it),
; blotchy floor patches at y=0.001, fixed-seed deterministic scatter within +/-0.42 tile-units
; of centre, +/-18% scale jitter and free Y-rotation, everything ground-level nested under one
; node named "Slab" (the OcclusionFader exemption convention). The human ruled on these values
; against Grass first precisely so they would not be re-proposed per terrain.
;
; HIGH-COUNT BLADES ARE A MULTIMESH; LOW-COUNT PROPS ARE INSTANCED glTF SCENES. Props here
; number 1-3 per tile, so a MultiMesh would buy nothing, and two of the flower meshes carry
; TWO surfaces with different textures, which a single embedded MultiMesh mesh cannot express
; cleanly. Referencing the raw piece directly is also what Meadow.tscn and Scrub.tscn already
; did before this pass.
;
; Source: Stylized Nature MegaKit (Standard/free), Quaternius, CC0 1.0 Universal — License.txt
; re-checked per asset-import-pipeline.md's audit gate. See
; project/attribution/sources/quaternius_stylized_nature_megakit.tres.
;
; GRASS COLOUR: DELIBERATELY DRIER BAND (2026-09-08 human ruling — "keep them drier").
; See GrassCommonShort.tscn's header for the full palette-band explanation. This terrain is
; deliberately NOT moved to band 2's true green: dryness is part of what distinguishes it from
; true Grass, and that distinction carries gameplay meaning (Scrub is `browse` rough grazing;
; Wild grass is tag-inert unclaimed land). It samples band 4, rgb(103,163,0) yellow-green —
; still a real change where the mesh shipped on band 1's gold, but visibly drier than Grass.
;
; OCCLUSIONFADER REMOVED 2026-09-08 — ANY MENTION OF IT BELOW IS HISTORY. The per-resident
; transparency fade (D-41 §4) flickered in play and was cut outright; the script, its scene node
; and its two suites are gone. The "Slab" node stays, because every terrain scene is built
; around it and removing it would restructure all 33 for no gain — but NO CODE LOOKS THAT NAME
; UP ANY MORE. It is a grouping convention now, with no behaviour attached, so nothing breaks if
; a new scene groups differently and nothing is gained by "restoring" the exemption.
[gd_scene format=4]

